.TH CLIOPort 1 "2026 August 28" ""

.SH NAME
CLIOPort \- I/O plugin tester application of the CoreLAB framework

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B clioport
[options]

.SH COPYRIGHT
CoreLAB is Copyright (C) 2026 by Pozsar Zsolt.

.SH DESCRIPTION
The CLIOPort application is intended for simple, manual testing of I/O port and
device simulator plugins of the CoreLAB modular framework. It allows loading the
plugin, viewing and modifying its properties, reading and writing the I/O port
directly, and saving and reloading the plugin state.
.PP
The program is designed for Windows and Unix-like operating systems.

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-d \-\-dir
Set plugin directory.
.TP
.B \-i \-\-ignore-help
Ignore missing help file or viewer.
.TP
.B \-h \-\-help
Show useable parameters.
.TP
.B \-v \-\-version
Show version and build information.

.SH OPERATION
.SS Plugin architecture
CLIOPort is designed for simple, manual testing of I/O port and device simulator
plugins used by the CoreLAB modular framework. Plugins are provided as
dynamically loadable shared libraries containing the plugin class implementation
and its exported entry points.
.PP
The base class for I/O port plugins is \fITIOPort\fP. A concrete plugin
implementation derives from this class and implements the device-specific
port operations and behaviour. Plugins requiring a graphical user interface
can derive from \fITGIOPort\fP, which extends \fITIOPort\fP with support for a
plugin-provided GUI panel.
.PP
When a plugin library is loaded, \fIclioport\fP resolves the required entry
points and creates an instance of the plugin class. The resulting object is
then used for port/device access and plugin management.
.PP
.SS Plugin interface
The plugin interface consists of the \fITIOPort\fP/\fITGIOPort\fP class
hierarchy and the exported plugin entry points.
.PP
The interface provides port read/write operations, reset and configuration,
interrupt handling, state saving and loading, and, for \fITGIOPort\fP
plugins, creation and management of the plugin GUI panel.
.PP
The main plugin properties include the address range, data-line configuration,
selector-line configuration, signal negation, enabled state, interrupt vector,
latched output and output read-back capabilities. Plugin identification and
description properties are also provided.

.SH ENVIRONMENTAL VARIABLES
.TP
.B LANG
This is the system language on Unix-like operating systems.

.SH FILES
.TP
.B ioport_*.dll, libioport_*.so :
The application loads processor plugins as shared libraries. On Windows,
plugins use the \fIioport_*.dll\fP naming convention; on Unix-like systems,
\fIlibioport_*.so\fP is used.
.TP
.B *.clpst:
Plugin state can be saved to and restored from CoreLAB stream files. The state
data is handled by the plugin through the corresponding state management
interface. Their content varies from plugin to plugin.

.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Normal exit.

